  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;The Company&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Baton Rouge Pipeline LLC (&amp;#x201C;Baton Rouge Pipeline&amp;#x201D;) is a Delaware limited liability company and a wholly owned&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;subsidiary of Baton Rouge Fractionators LLC, a Delaware limited liability company. Baton Rouge Fractionators LLC is owned 32.25% by Enterprise Products Operating LLC, a Texas limited liability company and 31.44% by Williams Field Services Group, LLC, a Delaware limited liability company. Effective 12/31/25, Amoco Louisiana Fractionator Company, a Delaware corporation, transferred its 19.44% membership interest in Baton Rouge Fractionators LLC to Exxon Chemical Louisiana LLC (Exxon), a Delaware limited liability company, which increased&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Exxon&amp;#x2019;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;total membership interest in Baton Rouge Fractionators LLC to 36.31%. Exxon physically operates Baton Rouge Pipeline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Description of the Property&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Baton Rouge Pipeline leases a 12" natural gas liquids (&amp;#x201C;NGL&amp;#x201D;) pipeline that is approximately 40 miles in length and located entirely within the State of Louisiana. The lease is recorded as a capital lease. The pipeline receives NGLs from a WILPRISE Pipeline Company, L.L.C.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;pipeline and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Exxon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;plants and storage wells and delivers NGLs to the Baton Rouge Fractionator located in West Baton Rouge Parish, Louisiana.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements conform to those required by FERC. Financial statements are prepared on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;the accrual&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt; basis of accounting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Baton Rouge Pipeline revenues are derived from transportation of NGLs under a tariff regulated by the FERC. The tariff specifies the amounts to be paid by shippers for service between receipt and delivery locations and the general terms and conditions of transportation services on the pipeline system. Revenues are recorded upon delivery of products to customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Baton Rouge Pipeline is a limited liability company that passes income tax liability through the company to its members and does not recognize this liability &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt; the company's financial statements. For purposes of calculating the income tax expense and liability for the annual cost of service (shown on page 700 of the Annual Report) Baton Rouge Pipeline employs FERC&amp;#x2019;s Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;Employees&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Baton Rouge Pipeline has no employees of its own. Field operations are performed by employees of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Exxon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;pursuant to an operating agreement. Management and administrative functions are performed by employees of Enterprise Products Company.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
